# AI session system (Multigres)

Borrowed from Multigres + Shamiri lab practice: **system + expertise + discipline**. The model types; we engineer. Full map: `docs/EAT-FISH-SPIT-BONES.md`.

## System (memory outside the chat)

- Durable truth: `AGENTS.md`, `docs/ENGINEERING.md`, `docs/STAGES.md`, `docs/EAT-FISH-SPIT-BONES.md`, `.kiro/context.md`
- Keep a stage checklist: task → expected output → command → evidence → status
- End meaningful work with a Fish-only STAGES handoff (what ran, what failed, next probe)
- After long threads/compaction: re-read STAGES + product law before coding more

## Expertise (know “right” first)

- Write expected status/body/Turso/R2 **before** interpreting results
- Presence Audit right = owned IG media + free diagnosis + gated fix, no fake uplift
- Voice Notes right = record **and** import persist to R2 + Turso
- Direction right = four answers → five structured ideas persisted
- Prefer extending existing OAuth/credit/R2 patterns over inventing parallel auth
- Local hacks that paper over design errors = Bones — fix root or mark debt

## Discipline

- Read critical path: route → service → Turso/R2 → credits
- Re-hit the real endpoint after “fixed”
- “Done?” → which command, which status, which DB/R2 field? No answer → not done
- Do not rubber-stamp STAGES PASS from agent narrative

## Anti-patterns

- Accepting Index Scan / “optimized” / “shipped” without a trace
- One mega-prompt instead of phased STAGES
- Editing working publish/OAuth “while here” without a reproduced bug
- Updating STAGES with unverified PASS
